<interfaces>
Contracts this plan creates; later plans (02-08 init, 02-14 spike, 02-15 Renovate) build against them.

bridge/entrypoint.sh modes (argument 1, default serve):
  serve         unlock keychain (fail closed, exit 78), start socat on <container IP>:1143 -> 127.0.0.1:1143,
                log the presented certificate's SPKI fingerprint in the background, exec bridge --noninteractive as uid 1000
  keychain-init idempotent: create the GPG key + pass store + canary when absent, then unlock and verify; prints "Bridge keychain ready"
  (02-08 adds: init, configure, cli, repair)
Exit codes: 0 ok, 64 unknown mode, 78 keychain/vault refusal (fixed messages, never the passphrase).
Process model: the entrypoint runs as root under tini; every gpg/pass/socat/bridge process runs as uid 1000 (user `bridge`) via `setpriv --reuid=1000 --regid=1000 --init-groups`. Root is kept only so 02-08's init can write the bind-mounted .env.mailboxes in place with its host owner and mode intact.
Container paths: /data (sift-bridge volume: HOME, GNUPGHOME=/data/.gnupg, PASSWORD_STORE_DIR=/data/.password-store, XDG_CONFIG_HOME=/data/config, XDG_DATA_HOME=/data/data, XDG_CACHE_HOME=/data/cache), /run/user/1000 (gpg-agent socket dir).
Only in the bridge-init service (D-79, D-81): /run/sift/.env.mailboxes (mailbox env file, read-write), /run/sift/config (config dir, read-only) and /run/sift/.env.mailboxes.bak (the host's pre-created backup file, read-write). In the bridge service none of these paths exists.
SPKI fingerprint format (shared with apps/worker/src/imap/pin.ts in 02-04 and the config value imap.tls.pin_sha256 in 02-02): base64 of sha256 over the DER SubjectPublicKeyInfo, i.e. `openssl x509 -pubkey -noout | openssl pkey -pubin -outform DER | openssl dgst -sha256 -binary | openssl base64 -A` (44 characters ending in `=`).

compose.yaml additions:
  services.bridge (Task 1): build ./bridge, image ${SIFT_BRIDGE_IMAGE:-sift-bridge:local},
    environment SIFT_BRIDGE_KEYCHAIN_PASSPHRASE: ${SIFT_BRIDGE_KEYCHAIN_PASSPHRASE:?set in .env},
    volumes: sift-bridge:/data only (D-79),
    ports "127.0.0.1:${SIFT_BRIDGE_PORT:-1143}:1143", TCP healthcheck, restart unless-stopped
  services.bridge-init (Task 2, D-79): the same build and image as bridge (so `docker compose run` builds it when absent), profiles ["tools"], command ["init"],
    the same SIFT_BRIDGE_KEYCHAIN_PASSPHRASE environment line,
    volumes: sift-bridge:/data, ${SIFT_MAILBOXES_ENV_FILE:-./.env.mailboxes}:/run/sift/.env.mailboxes, ${SIFT_CONFIG_HOST_DIR:-./config}:/run/sift/config:ro,
      and a long-syntax entry { type: bind, source: ./.env.mailboxes.bak, target: /run/sift/.env.mailboxes.bak } (D-81; no create_host_path, so a missing source fails),
    no ports, no healthcheck, restart "no".
    Compose v2.2.3 behaviour, probed during planning with a neutral file name: the long syntax parses; `docker compose run` of a profiled service needs no --profile flag;
    a missing long-syntax source fails with `bind source path does not exist` and creates nothing on the host; inside the container a rename onto the
    bind-mounted file fails with `Device or resource busy`, while an in-place truncate-and-write keeps the host file's inode and mode.
    Owner command: docker compose run --rm bridge-init. Other one-shot modes (02-08): docker compose run --rm bridge-init configure | cli | repair | keychain-init.
  volumes.sift-bridge: name ${SIFT_BRIDGE_VOLUME:-sift-bridge}, external: true
  No certificate volume, and no new worker or setup mounts: the pin lives in config.yaml (D-73).

Existing compose-smoke contract (scripts/compose-smoke.sh): dc() = docker compose --env-file "$smoke_env"; exports SIFT_PGDATA_VOLUME=<project>-pgdata-smoke and refuses sift-pgdata; generates .smoke/<project>/.env from .env.example filling `*_PASSWORD=` lines; `dc build` then `dc up -d`.
</interfaces>
