  </read_first>
  <action>
1. `bridge/Dockerfile` (RESEARCH Pattern 1, trial-built in research). Header comment: what the image is, that `apps/worker/test/bridge-image.test.ts` pins it, and that Renovate bumps BRIDGE_VERSION and BRIDGE_COMMIT together (D-31).
   - `# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1`, `ARG GO_VERSION=1.26.7`, build stage `FROM golang:${GO_VERSION}-trixie AS build`.
   - The three pin lines must be adjacent, in this order, because plan 02-15's Renovate regex matches them as one block: `# renovate: datasource=github-tags depName=ProtonMail/proton-bridge`, then `ARG BRIDGE_VERSION=v3.27.0`, then `ARG BRIDGE_COMMIT=04e46eb4fbc1c7ef4425a920bfc352050da0606b`.
   - One apt layer: `libfido2-dev libcbor-dev libsecret-1-dev libssl-dev pkg-config` with `--no-install-recommends` and list cleanup.
   - `git clone --depth 1 --branch "${BRIDGE_VERSION}"` of `https://github.com/ProtonMail/proton-bridge.git` into /src, then `test "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" = "${BRIDGE_COMMIT}"` in the same RUN so a moved tag fails the build.
   - `ENV GOTOOLCHAIN=local`, then `make build-nogui BRIDGE_APP_VERSION="${BRIDGE_VERSION#v}"` (assumption A8: Proton's API accepts this version string; the live spike confirms it).
   - Runtime stage `FROM debian:trixie-20260918-slim`, one apt layer: `ca-certificates libfido2-1 libsecret-1-0 pass gnupg socat openssl tini`. `setpriv` comes from util-linux in the base image; fail the build with `command -v setpriv` if it is missing.
   - Copy only `/src/bridge` to `/usr/local/bin/bridge`. Never copy the launcher binary: it is the self-update path that D-30 disables.
   - `useradd -m -u 1000 bridge`; `install -d -o bridge -g bridge -m 0700 /data /run/user/1000`; `install -d -m 0755 /run/sift`.
   - Copy `entrypoint.sh` to `/usr/local/bin/entrypoint.sh` (mode 0755). `EXPOSE 1143`. `ENTRYPOINT ["/usr/bin/tini", "--", "/usr/local/bin/entrypoint.sh"]`, `CMD ["serve"]`.
   - The image deliberately has no `USER` line: see the process model in the interfaces block. Add a comment saying so.
2. `bridge/entrypoint.sh` (`#!/bin/bash`, `set -euo pipefail`). Follow the interfaces block exactly.
   - Export HOME, GNUPGHOME, PASSWORD_STORE_DIR and XDG_CONFIG_HOME/XDG_DATA_HOME/XDG_CACHE_HOME under /data. The cache dir must stay inside the volume, because Bridge's single-instance lock lives there (RESEARCH Pattern 3).
   - Helper `as_bridge` runs a command via `setpriv --reuid=1000 --regid=1000 --init-groups` with those variables set.
   - `require_passphrase`: if SIFT_BRIDGE_KEYCHAIN_PASSPHRASE is empty or unset, print `SIFT_BRIDGE_KEYCHAIN_PASSPHRASE is not set; add it to .env` to stderr and exit 78.
   - `keychain_init` is idempotent. It writes `$GNUPGHOME/gpg-agent.conf` with `allow-preset-passphrase`, `max-cache-ttl 34560000` and `default-cache-ttl 34560000`. When no secret key exists it runs `gpg --batch --pinentry-mode loopback --passphrase-fd 0 --quick-gen-key sift-bridge-vault rsa3072 encr never`, feeding the passphrase on stdin (never as an argument). Then `pass init <fingerprint>`, then `pass insert -m sift/canary` with a fixed non-secret marker text.
   - `keychain_unlock`:
     - If no secret key exists, print `Bridge is not initialised: run docker compose run --rm bridge-init` and exit 78.
     - Start the agent with `gpg-connect-agent /bye`. Preset the passphrase for every keygrip from `gpg --list-secret-keys --with-keygrip --with-colons` using `$(gpgconf --list-dirs libexecdir)/gpg-preset-passphrase --preset`, with the passphrase on stdin.
     - Require `pass show sift/canary` to succeed, else print `Bridge keychain locked: check SIFT_BRIDGE_KEYCHAIN_PASSPHRASE` and exit 78.
     - Refuse an insecure vault: if `/data/config/protonmail/bridge-v3/insecure` exists, print `Insecure Bridge vault found; Sift refuses to run it. Remove the sift-bridge volume and run docker compose run --rm bridge-init again` and exit 78.
     - Then `unset SIFT_BRIDGE_KEYCHAIN_PASSPHRASE`.
   - `spki_fingerprint` reads a PEM on stdin and prints the fingerprint in the interfaces format.
   - `print_fingerprint`: wait up to 60 s for 127.0.0.1:1143, capture the certificate with `openssl s_client -starttls imap -connect 127.0.0.1:1143 </dev/null | openssl x509 -outform PEM`, then print `Bridge certificate SHA-256 (public key): <fingerprint>` (the value owners pin, D-73). Write no file.
   - Mode `serve`:
     - require_passphrase, then keychain_unlock.
     - Start socat as uid 1000 in the background: `socat TCP-LISTEN:1143,bind=<first field of hostname -i>,fork,reuseaddr TCP:127.0.0.1:1143`. Bind the container IP, never the wildcard address (Pitfall 1).
     - Start print_fingerprint in the background, then `exec` `bridge --noninteractive` through as_bridge.
     - Serve mode never reads /run/sift/.env.mailboxes or /run/sift/config; in the bridge service those paths do not exist (D-79).
   - Mode `keychain-init`: require_passphrase, keychain_init, keychain_unlock, print `Bridge keychain ready`, exit 0.
   - Any other mode: print the usage and exit 64.
   - Never echo the passphrase, and never use `set -x`.
3. `compose.yaml`: add the `bridge` service and the `sift-bridge` volume exactly as in the interfaces block (RESEARCH "Compose service shape", without the certificate volume).
   - Healthcheck: `["CMD", "bash", "-c", "exec 3<>/dev/tcp/127.0.0.1/1143"]`, interval 30s, timeout 5s, retries 3, start_period 60s, with no `start_interval`.
   - The ports comment reads "Loopback only. Never publish Bridge on all interfaces." Do not write the wildcard literal.
   - `restart: unless-stopped`. Do not add `depends_on: bridge` to the worker (D-32).
   - The bridge service mounts only `sift-bridge:/data`, with a comment: it never sees .env.mailboxes or config; the one-shot bridge-init service (added in Task 2) is the only service that does (D-39, D-79).
   - Extend the header comment:
     - Before the first `docker compose up`, run `docker volume create sift-bridge`. Compose v2.2.3 fails every command while an external volume is missing (Pitfall 3).
     - SIFT_BRIDGE_PORT moves the published port when the desktop Bridge app holds 1143 (Pitfall 11).
     - SIFT_BRIDGE_IMAGE and SIFT_BRIDGE_VOLUME exist only for the smoke scripts.
4. `.env.example`: add `SIFT_BRIDGE_KEYCHAIN_PASSPHRASE=` with a comment. Generate it with `openssl rand -hex 24`. Only the bridge container receives it. It unlocks the GPG key that protects Bridge's session vault in the sift-bridge volume, so a copied volume is useless without it. Losing it means running `docker compose run --rm bridge-init` again. Also add a commented `# SIFT_BRIDGE_PORT=1143`.
5. Developer machine, so later compose commands keep working:
   - Run `docker volume create sift-bridge`.
   - Append `SIFT_BRIDGE_KEYCHAIN_PASSPHRASE=<openssl rand -hex 24>` to the repository's real env file (the one compose reads), only if the key is absent. Use a scratchpad script that never prints the value. A Bash command whose text names the file is blocked (cerebrum).
6. `scripts/bridge-smoke.sh` (`set -euo pipefail`). Run it from the repo root; env BRIDGE_SMOKE_PORT (default 11143) and SIFT_BRIDGE_IMAGE (default sift-bridge:local).
   - `docker build -t "$image" bridge`.
   - Create a throwaway volume `sift-bridge-smoke-<random>`, with an EXIT trap that removes containers and the volume.
   - Run `keychain-init` with a random throwaway passphrase, then run `serve` detached, publishing `127.0.0.1:$BRIDGE_SMOKE_PORT:1143`.
   - Poll for up to 120 s until `openssl s_client -starttls imap -connect 127.0.0.1:$BRIDGE_SMOKE_PORT` prints `BEGIN CERTIFICATE`.
   - Compute that certificate's SPKI fingerprint with the openssl pipeline, and require the container log to contain `Bridge certificate SHA-256 (public key): <the same value>`.
   - Require exit 78 and `Bridge keychain locked` from `serve` with a wrong passphrase on the same volume.
   - Require exit 78 and `not initialised` from `serve` on a fresh empty volume.
   - Print `bridge smoke OK` last. Plans 02-08 and 02-15 extend and reuse it.
7. `apps/worker/test/bridge-image.test.ts` (style of node-version.test.ts; read files relative to the repo root):
   - Exactly one `ARG BRIDGE_VERSION=` line matching `^v3\.\d+\.\d+$`, and one `ARG BRIDGE_COMMIT=` line of 40 lowercase hex.
   - The renovate comment line sits directly above BRIDGE_VERSION, and BRIDGE_COMMIT directly below it.
   - The `git rev-parse HEAD` comparison and `GOTOOLCHAIN=local` are present.
   - No `COPY` line copies a path ending in `/proton-bridge`.
   - entrypoint.sh contains `pass show sift/canary`, `exit 78`, `bridge-v3/insecure`, `setpriv`, `bind=` and `Bridge certificate SHA-256 (public key)`.
   - No bridge file and no compose.yaml line contains the wildcard address. Build that regex from string parts so this test file does not contain the literal.
  </action>
  <verify>
    <automated>pnpm vitest run apps/worker/test/bridge-image.test.ts</automated>
