  <action>
0. `compose.yaml`: add the `bridge-init` service exactly as in the interfaces block (D-79, D-81).
   - It repeats bridge's `build` and `image`, so `docker compose run --rm bridge-init` builds the image when it is absent.
   - `profiles: ["tools"]` keeps `docker compose up` from ever starting it; `docker compose run` activates the profile of the service it targets, so the owner needs no `--profile` flag.
   - `command: ["init"]`, no ports, no healthcheck, `restart: "no"`.
   - The fourth volume entry is the long-syntax bind for the backup file (D-81): `type: bind`, `source: ./.env.mailboxes.bak`, `target: /run/sift/.env.mailboxes.bak`, with no `bind.create_host_path`. Its comment: the owner creates the file once with `touch .env.mailboxes.bak && chmod 600 .env.mailboxes.bak` (README quick start); long syntax makes a missing file stop Compose with `bind source path does not exist` instead of silently creating a directory; init writes the previous .env.mailboxes into it in place.
   - Comment above it: the one-time Bridge login and password setup (`docker compose run --rm bridge-init`); other one-shot modes run as `docker compose run --rm bridge-init configure|cli|repair`; it is the only service that sees .env.mailboxes and config, so the long-running bridge never does (D-39, D-79); stop the bridge service first, because Bridge allows one instance per vault.
   - Extend the header comment's first line to `db -> setup (one-shot) -> worker, plus bridge (and the one-shot bridge-init)`.
1. `scripts/compose-smoke.sh`:
   a. Build and start only the services the smoke checks: `dc build setup worker` and `dc up -d db setup worker`. The Bridge image is checked separately by scripts/bridge-smoke.sh. Update the header comment to match.
   b. Next to SIFT_PGDATA_VOLUME, export SIFT_BRIDGE_VOLUME=<project>-bridge-smoke.
   c. Refuse to run when it equals sift-bridge, with the same wording style as the sift-pgdata refusal.
   d. Run `docker volume create "$SIFT_BRIDGE_VOLUME"` before the first compose call.
   e. In the --down cleanup, remove that volume. `down -v` never removes external volumes.
   f. In the .env generation loop, also fill lines matching `*_PASSPHRASE=` with `openssl rand -hex 24`. When an existing smoke .env lacks a `SIFT_BRIDGE_KEYCHAIN_PASSPHRASE=` line, append one with a random value.
2. `apps/worker/test/compose.test.ts`:
   - Rename "defines db, setup and worker" to include bridge and bridge-init.
   - Add `describe('bridge service (D-29..D-38, D-73, D-79)')` asserting:
