     - volumes are exactly `sift-bridge:/data`: no volume entry targets /run/sift/.env.mailboxes or /run/sift/config, and no source names .env.mailboxes or config (D-79)
     - bridge has no `profiles` key, so `docker compose up` starts it
     - restart is unless-stopped and a healthcheck exists
   - Add `describe('bridge-init service (D-39, D-72, D-79)')` asserting:
     - profiles are exactly `['tools']` and command is exactly `['init']`
     - build context and image equal bridge's
     - volumes are exactly four entries, in order: `sift-bridge:/data`, `${SIFT_MAILBOXES_ENV_FILE:-./.env.mailboxes}:/run/sift/.env.mailboxes`, `${SIFT_CONFIG_HOST_DIR:-./config}:/run/sift/config:ro`, and the object `{ type: 'bind', source: './.env.mailboxes.bak', target: '/run/sift/.env.mailboxes.bak' }` with no `bind` key (so no create_host_path) (D-81)
     - no ports, and restart is `"no"`
   - Across all services:
     - the top-level sift-bridge volume has `external: true` and name `${SIFT_BRIDGE_VOLUME:-sift-bridge}`
     - only bridge and bridge-init mount sift-bridge
     - only bridge-init mounts anything under /run/sift (the env file, config and the backup file), and the bridge service's volumes are still exactly `['sift-bridge:/data']` (D-79, D-81)
     - Volume entries can now be strings or long-syntax objects: widen the test's ComposeFile type and make every existing helper that reads `volumes` handle both shapes
     - SIFT_BRIDGE_KEYCHAIN_PASSPHRASE appears in the bridge and bridge-init environments and in no other service
     - worker depends_on has no bridge or bridge-init key
     - worker and setup volumes are unchanged from Phase 1 (no certificate mount)
   - Keep the existing worker allowed-environment assertion unchanged.
