- `scripts/bridge-smoke.sh` ends with `bridge smoke OK`
- The compose smoke ends with `compose smoke OK`
</verification>

<success_criteria>
- Bridge runs in Compose from source at v3.27.0 / 04e46eb4 (D-29, D-30), reachable at bridge:1143 and host 127.0.0.1:1143 only
- The keychain fails closed: no passphrase, wrong passphrase, missing key or insecure vault means exit 78, never an unencrypted vault (D-38)
- Bridge logs the fingerprint owners pin in config (D-73); only the bridge and bridge-init containers mount the vault, and only bridge-init sees .env.mailboxes and config (D-72, D-79); the worker never depends on Bridge health (D-32)
</success_criteria>

## Artifacts this phase produces (this plan's share)

- Files: `bridge/Dockerfile`, `bridge/entrypoint.sh`, `scripts/bridge-smoke.sh`, `apps/worker/test/bridge-image.test.ts`; modified `compose.yaml`, `.env.example`, `scripts/compose-smoke.sh`, `apps/worker/test/compose.test.ts`, `apps/worker/test/compose-smoke.test.ts`
- Image: `sift-bridge:local` (`SIFT_BRIDGE_IMAGE`), entrypoint modes `serve`, `keychain-init`, exit code 78 for keychain or vault refusal
- Log line: `Bridge certificate SHA-256 (public key): <fingerprint>`
- Compose: service `bridge` with mount `/data` only; one-shot service `bridge-init` (profile `tools`, command `init`) with mounts `/data`, `/run/sift/.env.mailboxes`, `/run/sift/config` and the long-syntax backup bind `/run/sift/.env.mailboxes.bak` (D-81); external volume `sift-bridge` (`SIFT_BRIDGE_VOLUME`)
- Owner command: `docker compose run --rm bridge-init` (D-79)
- Env vars: `SIFT_BRIDGE_KEYCHAIN_PASSPHRASE` (bridge and bridge-init only), `SIFT_BRIDGE_PORT`, `SIFT_BRIDGE_IMAGE`, `SIFT_BRIDGE_VOLUME`, `BRIDGE_SMOKE_PORT`

## Flagged assumptions

- A8 (RESEARCH): Proton's API accepts `BRIDGE_APP_VERSION=3.27.0` from a source build. It cannot be tested without a login; the live spike (02-14) is the first real check.
- Bridge opens its IMAP listener before any account is logged in. Research probed this; scripts/bridge-smoke.sh fails loudly if it no longer holds.
- D-39's "bind-mounted read-write into the init run only" is met by D-79's separate bridge-init service; the earlier permanent mount on the bridge service is gone (T-02-06).
- Resolved by D-81: a single-file bind mount gives the container no writable host path beside the file (RESEARCH Pitfall 4), so bridge-init gets a fourth, long-syntax bind of the owner's pre-created `.env.mailboxes.bak`. The Compose v2.2.3 behaviour this relies on was probed during planning (see the interfaces block) and is re-checked by Task 2's `docker compose convert` command.

