    - packages/db/test/scope.test.ts (freshDatabase + seedMailboxes + app connection pattern)
    - .wolf/cerebrum.md (Drizzle 0.45 generic-table casts; empty .values([]) and .set({}) throw)
  </read_first>
  <action>
1. `scope.ts`, following the interfaces block:
   - Add `upsert` to scopedTable (and therefore to every ScopedTableApi). Reject `mailboxId` or `id` keys in rows or options with TypeError. Fill `mailboxId` into each row. Use `.onConflictDoUpdate({ target: [table.mailboxId, ...targetColumns], set })`, where set maps each `update` column to `sql\`excluded.<column>\`` and is otherwise a no-op assignment of the first target column to itself. `.returning({ id: table.id, inserted: sql<boolean>\`(xmax = 0)\` })`.
   - If drizzle refuses the composite target or `xmax` (assumption A1), fall back to `onConflictDoNothing` plus a select of the existing ids, keeping the same return contract.
   - Extend matchConditions: array values use `inArray`, and an empty array makes the helper return [] / 0 without running SQL.
   - Give `messageBody` an extra `deleteExpired(at)`: delete rows of this mailbox with `expires_at <= at`, return the count.
2. `ingest.ts`: start with `storeMessages`.
   - Strip `\u0000` from every string, including nested jsonb strings, with a local `stripNul` helper.
   - Upsert messages on target `['identityKey']` with no update columns.
   - When `promoteEligible` is set, set eligibleForClassification true for returned existing ids whose input is eligible and whose stored row is not, using `update({ eligibleForClassification: true }, { id: [...], eligibleForClassification: false })`.
   - Upsert locations on `['folder', 'uidvalidity', 'uid']` with update `['generation']`, mapping each item to its message id.
   - Upsert bodies on `['messageId']` with no update columns, only for items that supplied a body and whose stored message row is eligible. Read the eligibility of existing rows with find on id arrays.
   - Return StoreResult counts.
3. `index.ts`: export the ingest use-cases and their input types.
4. `ingest.test.ts`, on a fresh database clone with an app connection through createAppDb plus withMailbox:
   - Store two eligible items. Expect 2 message, 2 location and 2 body rows, insertedMessages 2.
   - Store the same items again. Counts are unchanged, and the result reports existingMessages 2, insertedLocations 0, insertedBodies 0.
  </action>
  <verify>
    <automated>pnpm vitest run packages/db/test/ingest.test.ts packages/db/test/scope.test.ts</automated>
    <fails_when>non-zero exit, a second storeMessages changing any row count, or any failed scope test</fails_when>
  </verify>
