  <behavior>
    - Same identity key in two items of one call: 1 message row, 2 location rows (D-14)
    - A historical item (eligible false) with a body supplied stores no body; storing it again eligible with promoteEligible makes it eligible and stores the body; without promoteEligible it stays historical
    - NUL characters in subject, a header value and an attachment name come back without NUL
    - getFolderSync returns null before createFolderSync and the row after; advanceFolderSync with a lower last_uid, an older watermark or a lower backfill cursor keeps the higher values, and a call that sets only the backfill cursor leaves last_uid and the watermark unchanged
    - createFolderSync with a backfill cursor stores all four backfill columns; setFolderBackfill(null) clears them; setFolderBackfill with a new cursor (after a resync) replaces them
    - markLocationsRemoved(ids, 'vanished') sets removed_at and removed_reason; liveLocations no longer lists them
    - deleteOrphanBodies keeps a body whose message still has another live location, keeps a body whose message has a decision row, and deletes it otherwise
    - beginResync sets state resyncing and both pending columns; finishResync with generation 2 marks generation-1 locations superseded where the message has a generation-2 location in that folder and vanished otherwise, deletes orphan bodies of the vanished ones, and leaves folder_sync with state ok, cleared pending columns, the new uidvalidity, last_uid and generation, and the persisted summary whose `gone` equals the vanished message count it returns
    - deleteExpiredBodies(at) deletes only expired rows, and none of another mailbox's
    - ISO-04: upsert and array match on a superuser (RLS-bypassing) handle touch only the scope's mailbox rows
