    - "normaliseMessageId strips surrounding whitespace and angle brackets and lowercases only the part after the last @; an empty, whitespace-only or `<>` value gives null, which falls through to the next key kind (D-13; SPK-03 empty edge)"
    - "Message-ID equality is byte-wise after D-13 normalisation; the local part is never case-folded, so `<A@x.org>` and `<a@x.org>` give different keys (SPK-03 encoding edge)"
    - "Header values are unfolded and RFC 2047-decoded with libmime, stripped of NUL, capped at 2000 characters and 20 values per name; stored text is cut on a code-point boundary and never splits a surrogate pair. Length means Unicode code points (ING-02 encoding edge)"
    - "A message with no text/plain part uses its text/html part converted by html-to-text; a message with neither gives body source `none` and empty text, not an error (D-06; ING-02 empty edge)"
    - "Body text is capped at 32768 code points with truncated = true when cut; the download is capped at 262144 bytes (D-06)"
    - "Attachments are recorded as name, MIME type and size only, at most 100 entries, names capped at 255 characters and NUL-stripped; no attachment content is read (D-06)"
    - "apps/worker/src/ingest/types.ts defines the FolderSource and IngestStore contracts that 02-09, 02-10 and 02-13 implement, with no imports from imapflow or @sift/db"
