---

<objective>
Define the ingest contracts (types only) that the IMAP adapter, the sync engine and the worker store build against. Implement the pure parsing step that turns one IMAP header record into an identity-keyed, size-capped `ParsedMessage` with body text and attachment metadata (D-06, D-12, D-13).

Purpose: identity is the one-way part of ingest (D-12). It must be deterministic, unit-tested on hostile input and free of I/O, so the spike (02-11) and the engine (02-10) share one implementation.

Output: `apps/worker/src/ingest/{types,identity,message}.ts` and their tests.
</objective>

