    - multipart/alternative with text/plain (part 1) and text/html (part 2) gives the text_plain part 1; HTML-only gives text_html with that part; image-only gives null
    - A text/plain part with disposition attachment is never chosen as the body
    - toBodyText(null, null) gives { text: '', source: 'none', truncated: false }
    - toBodyText of HTML `<p>Hello <b>there</b></p><script>x</script>` gives text containing "Hello there" and not "x" from the script
    - toBodyText of 40000 code points gives exactly 32768 code points and truncated true; text ending in an emoji at the boundary never ends in a lone surrogate
    - A download already marked truncated keeps truncated true even when the text is short
    - NUL inside body text is removed
    - attachmentsOf gives name (filename from disposition parameters, else the name parameter), MIME type `type/subtype` and size for parts with disposition attachment or a filename; 150 attachments are capped to 100; a 300-character name is capped to 255; NUL is stripped from names
    - parseMessage fills textPart and attachments from bodyStructure
  </behavior>
