<threat_model>
## Trust Boundaries

| Boundary | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| sender-controlled headers and bodies -> parser | Every byte is untrusted (SEC-01 groundwork) |

## STRIDE Threat Register

| Threat ID | Category | Component | Severity | Disposition | Mitigation Plan |
|-----------|----------|-----------|----------|-------------|-----------------|
| T-02-SC | Tampering | package installs | low | accept | No installs here (packages installed and approved in 02-04) |
| T-02-23 | Tampering | Forged Message-ID merging a new mail into an old row so it escapes classification | high | mitigate | pm: key from Bridge's overwritten X-Pm-Internal-Id wins for Bridge mailboxes; mid: is only a fallback; tested |
| T-02-24 | Denial of Service | Oversized headers, bodies or attachment lists | medium | mitigate | Value, count and text caps (2000 / 20 / 32768 code points / 100 attachments), 262144-byte download cap |
| T-02-25 | Tampering | Script or style content leaking into stored text | low | mitigate | html-to-text drops script/style; no HTML is stored |
</threat_model>

