## Artifacts this phase produces (this plan's share)

- Files: `apps/worker/src/ingest/types.ts`, `identity.ts`, `message.ts`; tests `ingest-identity.test.ts`, `ingest-message.test.ts`
- Types: `FolderStatus`, `UidDate`, `AddressLite`, `EnvelopeLite`, `BodyNode`, `HeaderRecord`, `TextPart`, `FolderSource`, `AttachmentMeta`, `ParsedMessage`, `BodyText`, `MessageRecord`, `BackfillState`, `FolderState`, `ChunkAdvance`, `ResyncCounts`, `LiveLocationRef`, `IngestStore`, `IngestOutcome`, `IngestLog`
- Functions and constants: `normaliseMessageId`, `stableHeaderHash`, `identityKey`, `stripNul`, `truncateCodePoints`, `HDR_HASH_INPUTS`, `HEADER_FIELDS`, `parseHeaderBlock`, `parseMessage`, `selectTextPart`, `attachmentsOf`, `toBodyText`, `BODY_TEXT_MAX_CHARS`, `BODY_DOWNLOAD_MAX_BYTES`, `HEADER_VALUE_MAX_CHARS`, `HEADER_VALUES_MAX`, `ATTACHMENTS_MAX`, `ATTACHMENT_NAME_MAX_CHARS`

## Edge coverage carried by this plan

- SPK-03 empty (resolved, explicit): a missing or empty Message-ID normalises to null and falls through to the next key kind.
- SPK-03 encoding (resolved, explicit): equality is byte-wise after D-13 normalisation, and the local part is never case-folded.
- ING-02 encoding (resolved, explicit): RFC 2047 is decoded, NUL stripped, and lengths are counted in code points with no split surrogates.
- ING-02 empty (resolved, explicit): no text part gives body source `none` with empty text.

## Flagged assumptions

- A6 (RESEARCH): the `hdr:` hash inputs (Date, From, To, Cc, Subject, In-Reply-To plus size). The live spike (02-14) confirms or changes them before real mail is stored. Bridge synthesises a Message-ID when one is missing, so hdr: keys should be rare for Bridge mailboxes.

