  configure  require_passphrase, keychain_unlock, check /run/sift/.env.mailboxes (absent: exit 2 with the bridge-init hint; not a regular file: exit 2 with the create-first message),
             start `bridge --grpc` as uid 1000 in the background,
             wait for its gRPC server config file, print the certificate fingerprint plus the paste hint (D-73), run `sift-helper configure` as root,
             then wait for Bridge to exit after the helper's Quit.
             Exit codes: 0 at least one mailbox written, 2 env file absent or not a regular file, or the backup cannot be written, 3 no Bridge account logged in,
             4 no configured mailbox matches a Bridge address, 78 keychain/vault.
  init       requires a TTY; keychain_init, keychain_unlock, run `bridge --cli` as uid 1000 attached to the TTY (owner types `login`, then `exit`), then configure.
  cli        requires a TTY; keychain_unlock, `bridge --cli` (owner maintenance such as logout).
  repair     no TTY needed; require_passphrase, keychain_unlock, start `bridge --grpc` in the background, `sift-helper repair` (gRPC TriggerRepair),
             wait 30 s, then the helper's Quit; Bridge rebuilds its IMAP cache on the next `serve` start (used by the live spike, D-43).
Fingerprint output of configure:
  Bridge certificate SHA-256 (public key): <fingerprint>
  Add it to config/config.yaml under the mailbox's imap.tls:   pin_sha256: <fingerprint>

sift-helper (Go, copied into the Bridge tree as cmd/sift-helper so it can import internal/frontend/grpc, RESEARCH Pattern 3):
  sift-helper configure --config /run/sift/config/config.yaml --env-file /run/sift/.env.mailboxes --backup /run/sift/.env.mailboxes.bak
    (/run/sift/.env.mailboxes.bak is the host's .env.mailboxes.bak as seen inside bridge-init, D-79; see Flagged assumptions for how it is mapped)
    reads the gRPC server config ({port, cert, token, fileSocketPath}; confirm its file name and directory in the pinned source),
    connects over the unix socket with TLS (RootCAs = config cert, ServerName 127.0.0.1) and `server-token` metadata,
    SetIsTelemetryDisabled(true), SetIsAutomaticUpdateOn(false), reads both back and prints `telemetry: off`, `automatic updates: off`,
    GetUserList; prints `accounts: <n>` and, per account, `addresses: <count>, address mode: combined|split` (never the addresses),
    matches mailboxes (slug, imap.username, imap.password_env from config.yaml) to accounts by address, case-insensitively,
    before the first write calls BackupInPlace with the current env file's bytes and prints `backup of the previous file: .env.mailboxes.bak (next to .env.mailboxes)`;
    if that fails it writes nothing and exits 2 with `cannot write the backup .env.mailboxes.bak; nothing was written. Create it once on the host: touch .env.mailboxes.bak && chmod 600 .env.mailboxes.bak`; then upserts NAME=password lines (envfile.go),
    prints `wrote <NAME> to .env.mailboxes (mailbox "<slug>")` per mailbox,
    prints `mailbox "<slug>": no Bridge account has its address; nothing written` for unmatched ones, calls Quit, exits 0/3/4 as above.
  sift-helper repair
    connects the same way, calls TriggerRepair (confirm the RPC name in bridge.proto), prints `repair triggered`, waits 30 s, calls Quit, exits 0.
envfile.go:
  func UpsertEnv(content []byte, updates []EnvVar) (out []byte, err error)   // EnvVar{Name, Value}; Name must match ^[A-Z_][A-Z0-9_]*$, Value must not contain CR, LF or NUL
  func WriteInPlace(path string, content []byte) error                        // refuses missing and non-regular files; opens the EXISTING file write-only with truncate (no create flag), writes, fsyncs;
                                                                              // never a temp file, never rename: a rename onto a bind-mounted file fails with EBUSY or detaches it (D-81)
  func BackupInPlace(path string, content []byte) error                       // the owner's pre-created backup file (D-81): refuses a missing or non-regular path; WriteInPlace, then chmod 0600
</interfaces>
</context>

