  <behavior>
    - UpsertEnv on "A=1\n# c\nB=2\n" with B=x and C=y gives "A=1\n# c\nB=x\nC=y\n"; a duplicate later `B=` line is removed; a file without a trailing newline gains one; CRLF input stays parseable
    - UpsertEnv rejects a lowercase name, and a value containing a newline, CR or NUL, with an error that names the variable and not the value
    - WriteInPlace refuses a directory and keeps the file's mode (0600 stays 0600)
    - BackupInPlace refuses a missing path and a directory; on an existing regular file it writes the previous bytes exactly and leaves mode 0600
    - WriteInPlace and BackupInPlace keep the target's inode: syscall.Stat_t Ino is the same before and after, on files that held longer content than the new bytes (truncation proven)
    - configure with a missing or directory backup target exits 2, its message contains `touch .env.mailboxes.bak && chmod 600 .env.mailboxes.bak`, and the env file is byte-identical afterwards
    - Static (bridge-image.test.ts): the non-test Go files under bridge/helper contain no rename call, no temp-file creation and no create flag; and git ignores a file named .env.mailboxes.bak at the repository root (git check-ignore run through execFile from the test)
    - configure with nothing mounted at /run/sift/.env.mailboxes (the bridge service's shape) exits 2 with `run this in the bridge-init service: docker compose run --rm bridge-init`
    - configure with a directory mounted at /run/sift/.env.mailboxes exits 2 with `create .env.mailboxes first: cp .env.mailboxes.example .env.mailboxes`
    - init without a TTY (`docker run -i`, no -t) exits 2 with `init needs an interactive terminal: docker compose run --rm bridge-init`
    - A sentinel value placed in the mounted env file never appears in the container's stdout or stderr during configure
  </behavior>
