<threat_model>
## Trust Boundaries

| Boundary | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| owner terminal -> Bridge CLI | Proton password and 2FA typed during init |
| Bridge gRPC frontend -> sift-helper | IMAP password bytes inside the container |
| container -> host .env.mailboxes (bind mount) | Secret written to the host |
| Bridge -> Proton telemetry and update endpoints | Data leaving the machine |

## STRIDE Threat Register

| Threat ID | Category | Component | Severity | Disposition | Mitigation Plan |
|-----------|----------|-----------|----------|-------------|-----------------|
| T-02-SC | Tampering | Go module resolution for sift-helper (yaml.v3, grpc) | medium | mitigate | Only modules already in Bridge's pinned go.mod/go.sum; any go mod download is checksum-verified; no npm/pip/cargo installs |
| T-02-26 | Information Disclosure | IMAP password shown in terminal or logs | high | mitigate | Helper prints only `wrote NAME ...` lines; values validated and never echoed in errors; sentinel check in bridge-smoke.sh |
| T-02-27 | Information Disclosure | Bridge telemetry on by default | high | mitigate | SetIsTelemetryDisabled(true), read back and printed; verified by bridge-smoke.sh |
| T-02-28 | Tampering | Automatic update replacing the pinned Bridge | medium | mitigate | SetIsAutomaticUpdateOn(false) read back; launcher never shipped (02-01) |
| T-02-29 | Spoofing | Owner pinning a fingerprint they did not see from their own Bridge | medium | mitigate | init prints the fingerprint at login time; `sift bridge trust` (02-15) shows what the worker sees, so the owner compares two independent readings (D-73) |
| T-02-30 | Tampering | .env.mailboxes clobbered or replaced by a directory | medium | mitigate | Regular-file check (exit 2), 0600 host-side backup `.env.mailboxes.bak` before writing and no write without it (D-79), in-place write without temp file or rename into the existing files, inode and mode preserved (D-81); tested |
| T-02-61 | Information Disclosure | Host-side `.env.mailboxes.bak` holding Bridge IMAP passwords | medium | mitigate | BackupInPlace forces mode 0600; the repository's `.env.*` ignore rule keeps it out of git (git-ignore case in bridge-image.test.ts); the owner pre-creates it with mode 600 (D-81); the output and README name the file so the owner can clear it (D-79) |
</threat_model>

<verification>
- `docker build -q bridge` succeeds (includes `go test ./cmd/sift-helper/...`)
- `scripts/bridge-smoke.sh` ends with `bridge smoke OK` (serve, refusal, configure and repair checks)
- `pnpm vitest run apps/worker/test/bridge-image.test.ts` passes
</verification>

<success_criteria>
- D-72/D-79: `docker compose run --rm bridge-init` is the whole owner-facing setup; only the bridge and bridge-init containers touch the vault, and only bridge-init sees .env.mailboxes
- D-36/D-39: the owner logs in once through Bridge's own CLI; the IMAP password lands only in .env.mailboxes (plus its host-side backup .env.mailboxes.bak, D-79)
- D-73: init prints the fingerprint to pin; nothing is trusted automatically
- Telemetry and automatic updates are off (PROJECT privacy constraint, D-30)
</success_criteria>

## Artifacts this phase produces (this plan's share)

- Files: `bridge/helper/main.go`, `bridge/helper/envfile.go`, `bridge/helper/envfile_test.go`; modified `bridge/Dockerfile`, `bridge/entrypoint.sh`, `scripts/bridge-smoke.sh`, `apps/worker/test/bridge-image.test.ts`
- Binary: `/usr/local/bin/sift-helper` with subcommands `configure --config <path> --env-file <path> --backup <path>` and `repair`
- Go symbols: `UpsertEnv`, `WriteInPlace`, `BackupInPlace`, `EnvVar`
- Entrypoint modes: `init`, `configure`, `cli`, `repair`; exit codes 2 (env file or TTY), 3 (no account), 4 (no mailbox matched)
- Owner command: `docker compose run --rm bridge-init`
- Host file: `.env.mailboxes.bak` next to `.env.mailboxes` (previous content, 0600; D-79)

## Flagged assumptions

- A7 (RESEARCH): an in-tree `cmd/sift-helper` may import `internal/frontend/grpc`. If the pinned tree refuses, vendor bridge.proto and generate a client with protoc in the build stage instead.
- Bridge's gRPC frontend serves its config file and accepts calls with no GUI attached, and TriggerRepair exists under that name. Task 1's smoke run proves both; a hang hits the 90 s timeout message.
- Resolved by D-81: the owner pre-creates `.env.mailboxes.bak` (`touch .env.mailboxes.bak && chmod 600 .env.mailboxes.bak`, README quick start), and 02-01 bind-mounts it into bridge-init only, in long syntax, at /run/sift/.env.mailboxes.bak. A probe on this machine's Compose v2.2.3 (neutral file name) showed that a rename onto a bind-mounted file fails with `Device or resource busy`, and an in-place truncate-and-write keeps the host inode and mode, which is why both files are written in place.

