  truths:
    - "A folder's first sync records UIDVALIDITY, last_uid = UIDNEXT - 1 and watermark = now. With initial_backfill_days N > 0 it also records a backfill cursor over the mail whose INTERNALDATE falls in the last N days; with N = 0, or an empty folder, there is no backfill and nothing fails (D-74, D-75; ING-03 empty edge)"
    - "The first backfill is not stopped by the cap. Each cycle processes at most one slice (default 200 messages), in chunks with a pause between them, after the cycle's new-mail work; it reports done/total progress; it continues across cycles and restarts from its cursor, and finishes by clearing the cursor (D-75)"
    - "Backfilled messages are stored as eligible with bodies, and a historical row inside the window is promoted to eligible (D-75, D-21)"
    - "Mail that arrives after the start point is stored on the next run: one message row per identity, its location and a body for eligible mail; running again stores nothing more (ING-02, ING-03)"
    - "When UIDNEXT <= last_uid + 1 the engine issues no header FETCH for new mail; records at or below last_uid that `n:*` returns are dropped, so the newest old message is never re-processed (ING-03 adjacency and empty edges)"
    - "Messages are processed in ascending UID order in chunks of 50, each chunk committed with its cursor advanced to the chunk's highest UID; an abort between chunks returns `aborted` and the next run continues after the last committed chunk with no duplicates (D-04; ING-02 ordering edge)"
    - "A message polled as new counts as new only when its INTERNALDATE is strictly later than (watermark - 5 minutes). Equal to the boundary or older means historical: message row and location, not eligible, no body (D-18..D-21; ING-02 adjacency edge) (D-20: an old message moved back into the folder keeps its INTERNALDATE and stays historical)"
    - "Mail arriving while a cycle runs is picked up by the next cycle; the watermark only moves forward, to the latest INTERNALDATE of eligible new mail processed (D-18; ING-03 ordering edge)"
    - "If more messages than ingest.new_mail_cap would be new in one polling cycle or one resync, the run returns needs_attention with the count and stores nothing new (D-26, D-75)"
    - "countBackfill(days) reports how many messages a CLI backfill would ingest; runBackfill(days) ingests exactly those as eligible without moving last_uid, the watermark or the first-backfill cursor, with no cap, and refuses while the folder is resyncing or before its first sync (D-75)"
    - "A stored live location whose UID is no longer in the folder is marked vanished and its never-classified body is deleted (D-07, D-17)"
    - "On a UIDVALIDITY change the folder is marked resyncing and rescanned headers-only in batches of 500: known keys get a new-generation location, unknown new mail is processed normally, unknown old mail becomes historical, and nothing is re-created or reclassified. A pending first backfill restarts under the new UIDVALIDITY and promotes what it finds (D-22, D-24, D-75)"
    - "A resync that fails part-way leaves the previous generation authoritative; the next run retries from the start with the same pending generation (or a fresh one if UIDVALIDITY changed again) and completes with the same counts (D-23)"
    - "A finished resync persists and logs `<folder> resynced: <matched> matched, <new> new, <gone> gone, <older> older than backfill window`, with thousands separators (D-25)"
