<threat_model>
## Trust Boundaries

| Boundary | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| IMAP server state (UIDs, dates, UIDVALIDITY) -> ingest decisions | A misbehaving or rebuilding server must not cause mass processing |

## STRIDE Threat Register

| Threat ID | Category | Component | Severity | Disposition | Mitigation Plan |
|-----------|----------|-----------|----------|-------------|-----------------|
| T-02-SC | Tampering | package installs | low | accept | No installs in this plan |
| T-02-34 | Denial of Service | Bridge cache rebuild or UIDVALIDITY reset presenting thousands of "new" UIDs | high | mitigate | INTERNALDATE gate on polling and resync, and the volume valve before any write (D-19, D-26); tested with renumbered UIDs |
| T-02-35 | Tampering | Partial resync corrupting location state | medium | mitigate | Generation tagging; the previous generation stays authoritative until finishResync in one transaction; retry tested (D-23) |
| T-02-36 | Denial of Service | A 30-day first backfill starving new mail or Bridge | medium | mitigate | Per-cycle slice (200), pause between chunks, run after new-mail work each cycle (D-75) |
| T-02-37 | Information Disclosure | Engine logs leaking mail content | medium | mitigate | Logs carry counts, UIDs and folder names only; identity keys and subjects are never logged |
</threat_model>

<verification>
- `pnpm vitest run apps/worker/test/ingest-engine.test.ts apps/worker/test/ingest-resync.test.ts` passes
- `pnpm lint && pnpm typecheck` exits 0
</verification>

<success_criteria>
- ING-02/ING-03: new mail is stored exactly once, on the next poll, resumably
- ING-04: a UIDVALIDITY change gives a safe resync with no duplicates and no reclassification
- D-26/D-75: polling and resync surges stop the mailbox; the first backfill runs throttled and uncapped with progress; the CLI backfill is count-first and uncapped
</success_criteria>

## Artifacts this phase produces (this plan's share)

- Files: `apps/worker/src/ingest/plan.ts`, `apps/worker/src/ingest/run.ts`, `apps/worker/test/support/fake-folder-source.ts`, `apps/worker/test/support/fake-ingest-store.ts`, `apps/worker/test/ingest-engine.test.ts`, `apps/worker/test/ingest-resync.test.ts`
- Symbols: `runIngest`, `countBackfill`, `runBackfill`, `IngestDeps`, `BackfillOutcome`, `BackfillRefusedError`, `CHUNK_SIZE` (50), `RESYNC_BATCH_SIZE` (500), `WATERMARK_OVERLAP_MS` (300000), `BACKFILL_SLICE_SIZE` (200), `BACKFILL_CHUNK_PAUSE_MS` (250), `isCandidateNew`, `aboveLastUid`, `chunk`, `pendingGenerationFor`, `backfillWindow`, `formatResyncLine`, `FakeFolderSource`, `FakeIngestStore`
- Log line: `<folder> resynced: <matched> matched, <new> new, <gone> gone, <older> older than backfill window`

## Edge coverage carried by this plan

- ING-02 ordering (resolved, explicit): ascending UID order, and each cursor (last_uid, backfill cursor) advances monotonically per committed chunk.
- ING-02 adjacency, watermark boundary (resolved, explicit): strict `>` against watermark - 5 min; equal means historical.
- ING-03 adjacency (resolved, explicit): `n:*` records at or below last_uid are dropped.
- ING-03 empty (resolved, explicit): no FETCH when UIDNEXT <= last_uid + 1; an empty folder's first sync records the start point with no backfill.
- ING-03 ordering (resolved, explicit): mail arriving mid-cycle is taken by the next cycle; the watermark only moves forward.

## Flagged assumptions

- ING-04 (edge probe: unclassified, unresolved). "Safe full resync" is taken to mean the D-23 generation scheme: all-or-nothing, previous generation authoritative until completion, retry from the start, nothing reclassified. The live spike tests whether INTERNALDATE survives a Bridge cache rebuild (D-43). If it does not, the findings must change D-18/D-22, and this engine gets a gap-closure plan.
- Pitfall 6 / A4: Bridge may assign UIDs above Sift's start point to old mail during its initial sync. The INTERNALDATE gate makes that harmless on the polling path; the spike notes whether it happens.
- D-75 "throttled at low priority" is implemented as a per-cycle slice (200 messages) with a 250 ms pause between chunks, run after the cycle's new-mail work. Both values are constants the owner can ask to change.

