<task type="checkpoint:human-action" gate="blocking">
  <name>Task 2: Owner logs Bridge in to the real Proton account and approves the bounded test steps</name>
  <action>Log Proton Bridge in once (Proton password and 2FA cannot be automated), and approve the mailbox-touching spike steps</action>
  <instructions>
Claude has built the Bridge and worker images and initialised the Bridge keychain. Please do the following from the main repository folder.

1. If the desktop Proton Mail Bridge app is running, quit it (it holds port 1143).
2. Edit `config/config.yaml` so it has one mailbox with your Proton address:
   - slug `personal`
   - `imap.host: bridge`, `imap.port: 1143`
   - `imap.username: <your Proton address>`
   - `imap.password_env: SIFT_PERSONAL_IMAP_PASSWORD`
   - `folder: INBOX`
   - `labels.apply_as: proton_labels`
   - `ingest.initial_backfill_days: 0` for the spike, so nothing is ingested while the probe runs (set it back to the value you want before the end-of-phase worker run)
3. Run `docker compose run --rm bridge-init` (Claude has already created the empty backup file `.env.mailboxes.bak` with mode 600; D-81). At the Bridge prompt type `login`, then your Proton address, password and 2FA code, then `exit`. Expected lines:
   - `telemetry: off`
   - `automatic updates: off`
   - `accounts: 1`
   - `addresses: <n>, address mode: combined`
   - `backup of the previous file: .env.mailboxes.bak (next to .env.mailboxes)`
   - `wrote SIFT_PERSONAL_IMAP_PASSWORD to .env.mailboxes (mailbox "personal")`
   - `Bridge certificate SHA-256 (public key): <fingerprint>`, then the `pin_sha256: <fingerprint>` line
   No password should appear anywhere.
4. Paste that line into `config/config.yaml` under the mailbox's `imap.tls:` block (`pin_sha256: <fingerprint>`).
5. Reply with one of:
   - `done: full`: Claude may (a) wait for one new email in INBOX, copy that one message into a new label `Labels/Sift Spike` and remove it from that label again, and (b) force a Bridge repair, which rebuilds Bridge's local cache. After replying, send yourself ONE short test email within 10 minutes; it is the only message Sift will label.
   - `done: no-repair`: as above without (b).
   - `done: read-only`: no label test and no repair; Claude only reads.
   Add the address mode line from step 3 to your reply.
  </instructions>
  <verification>`docker compose run --rm --no-deps -T worker sift config check` prints a line starting `Config OK: 1 mailboxes (personal)`; config.yaml has a pin_sha256 for the mailbox; a presence-only script confirms SIFT_PERSONAL_IMAP_PASSWORD is set in .env.mailboxes</verification>
  <read_first>
    - .planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-08-SUMMARY.md (init output format)
  </read_first>
  <acceptance_criteria>
    - The owner's reply is one of `done: full`, `done: no-repair`, `done: read-only` and includes the address mode; it is recorded verbatim in 02-14-SUMMARY.md
  </acceptance_criteria>
  <resume-signal>Reply "done: full", "done: no-repair" or "done: read-only", plus the address mode line</resume-signal>
</task>

<task type="auto">
  <name>Task 3: Run the approved probes, then write the findings, the ADR-0003 addendum and the doc-contract test</name>
  <files>.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-SPIKE-FINDINGS.md, docs/adr/0003-traces-and-mail-app-relabels.md, apps/worker/test/spike-findings.test.ts</files>
  <read_first>
    - .planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-14-SUMMARY.md draft (owner reply from Task 2)
    - .planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-RESEARCH.md "Pre-spike evidence" table (what to confirm or refute) and "Spike probe design" step 7
    - .planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-CONTEXT.md D-09, D-12..D-18, D-22, D-27, D-35, D-43
    - docs/adr/0003-traces-and-mail-app-relabels.md
  </read_first>
  <action>
Run from the main checkout. Probe output goes only to data/spike/ (git-ignored); never print a report body to the terminal beyond counts.
1. `docker compose run --rm setup` (registers the mailbox), then `docker compose up -d bridge`, and wait for `healthy`.
   - Bridge first syncs the account. Run `sift bridge probe personal` every 60 s with stdout to data/spike/probe-0-sync-<n>.json.
   - Record whether login worked while syncing and whether UIDNEXT grew during the sync (RESEARCH A4, Pitfall 6).
   - Stop when UIDNEXT is unchanged for two consecutive probes, or after 30 minutes.
2. Baseline: `docker compose run --rm --no-deps -T worker sift bridge probe personal --sample 20 > data/spike/probe-1-baseline.json`.
3. For `done: full` or `done: no-repair`: `printf 'LABEL\n' | docker compose run --rm --no-deps -T worker sift bridge probe personal --wait-new-seconds 600 --label-test > data/spike/probe-2-label.json`. If no new mail arrived, record that the label test was skipped and why.
4. Restart: `docker compose restart bridge`, wait for healthy, then `docker compose run --rm --no-deps -T worker sift bridge probe personal --compare - < data/spike/probe-1-baseline.json > data/spike/probe-3-restart.json`.
5. For `done: full`:
   - `docker compose stop bridge`.
   - Run `docker compose run --rm --no-deps -T bridge-init configure` to capture the `accounts`, `addresses` and `address mode` lines. They contain no secrets, and it rewrites the same password line.
   - `docker compose run --rm --no-deps -T bridge-init repair`, then `docker compose up -d bridge`.
   - Wait for the cache rebuild as in step 1.
   - `... sift bridge probe personal --compare - < data/spike/probe-1-baseline.json > data/spike/probe-4-repair.json`.
6. Write `02-SPIKE-FINDINGS.md` from the reports, with these sections. Aggregates only: counts, booleans, capability atoms, UID and UIDVALIDITY numbers, durations.
   - `## Labels as folders (SPK-01)`: prefixes, delimiter and counts; apply = UID COPY into `Labels/<name>`; remove = \Deleted plus UID EXPUNGE in the label folder; whether the INBOX copy survived both; whether COPYUID came back.
   - `## CONDSTORE and QRESYNC (SPK-02)`: pre- and post-auth capabilities; ENABLE and STATUS results.
   - `## Message identity (SPK-03)`:
     - X-Pm-Internal-Id presence and equality across the INBOX and label copies
     - Message-ID byte equality
     - missing (protonmail.internalid) and duplicate counts
     - date skew
     - a line `**Identity key:**` confirming `pm:` first, then `mid:`, then `hdr:`, or stating the change
     - the hdr: inputs (A6) confirmed or changed
   - `## UIDVALIDITY and INTERNALDATE (SPK-04)`: restart and repair comparisons; a line `**D-18/D-22 design:** stands` or the change it needs.
   - `## IDLE`.
   - `## Address mode`: combined confirmed or not (D-35).
   - `## Decision for later phases`:
     - a line `**Sync capability to assume:** <polling only | CONDSTORE | QRESYNC>`
     - a line `**Phase 4 label application:**` (apply method, remove method, record the label-folder UID from COPYUID for echo suppression, pause while folder_sync is resyncing)
     - a line for M2 relabel detection
   - `## Method`: versions, commands, dates, and which steps the owner approved.
   - Remove "Status: in progress".
7. ADR-0003: append `## Addendum (2026-10): Proton Bridge spike (M1)`:
   - link `.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-SPIKE-FINDINGS.md`
   - restate the sync-capability decision, the identity decision (Bridge's internal ID first) and the label apply/remove method
   - resolve the raw-prompt retention item: traces store the prompt recipe (prompt and rule-set versions plus example Message-IDs), not raw prompts, while the LLM's raw output stays in the trace (D-09)
8. `apps/worker/test/spike-findings.test.ts` reads both files and asserts:
   - every section heading above exists
   - the `**Sync capability to assume:**` line ends in one of the three allowed values
   - `**Phase 4 label application:**` and `**Identity key:**` lines exist
   - no line starts with Subject:, From: or To: (case-insensitive)
   - no email address appears except on the allowlisted domains example.test and protonmail.internalid
   - the ADR contains `## Addendum` and the findings path
  </action>
  <verify>
    <automated>pnpm vitest run apps/worker/test/spike-findings.test.ts</automated>
    <fails_when>non-zero exit: a missing section or decision line, a disallowed email address or header line in either document, or a missing ADR addendum</fails_when>
  </verify>
  <acceptance_criteria>
    - `grep -cE '^\*\*Sync capability to assume:\*\* (polling only|CONDSTORE|QRESYNC)' .planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-SPIKE-FINDINGS.md` prints 1
    - `grep -n '## Addendum' docs/adr/0003-traces-and-mail-app-relabels.md` matches
    - `git check-ignore -q data/spike/probe-1-baseline.json` exits 0, and `git status --porcelain data/` prints nothing
    - spike-findings.test.ts passes
  </acceptance_criteria>
  <done>The Bridge questions are answered from the real mailbox. Later phases have a written decision to build on, and no mail content left the git-ignored data directory.</done>
