   - One customManager: `customType: "regex"`, `managerFilePatterns: ["/^bridge/Dockerfile$/"]`, and a matchStrings entry capturing datasource and depName from the renovate comment, then `ARG BRIDGE_VERSION=(?<currentValue>\S+)` and `ARG BRIDGE_COMMIT=(?<currentDigest>[0-9a-f]{40})` across the adjacent lines (RESEARCH example).
   - `packageRules: [{ matchDepNames: ["ProtonMail/proton-bridge"], ignoreUnstable: true }]`.
   - Record in the SUMMARY (not in the JSON) that `github-tags` filling currentDigest with the tag's commit is assumption A2. If a bump changes only the tag, the build's commit check fails the PR, which is the intended fail-safe.
2. `.github/workflows/bridge-image.yml`:
   - name `bridge-image`, `permissions: contents: read`, concurrency per ref.
   - One job on ubuntu-24.04 with timeout-minutes 30: checkout pinned to the same SHA and comment as ci.yml, then `scripts/bridge-smoke.sh`.
3. `bridge-image.test.ts`: add the behavior cases. Read renovate.json, convert the matchStrings entry with `new RegExp(...)` (JS named groups use the same syntax) and parse the workflow with `yaml`.
  </action>
  <verify>
    <automated>pnpm vitest run apps/worker/test/bridge-image.test.ts apps/worker/test/ci-workflow.test.ts && actionlint .github/workflows/bridge-image.yml</automated>
    <fails_when>non-zero exit: the regex not matching the Dockerfile or capturing the wrong values, an unpinned action, or actionlint diagnostics</fails_when>
  </verify>
  <acceptance_criteria>
    - `grep -n '"enabledManagers"' renovate.json` matches and lists only `custom.regex`
    - `grep -nE 'uses: actions/checkout@[0-9a-f]{40}' .github/workflows/bridge-image.yml` matches
    - `grep -n 'scripts/bridge-smoke.sh' .github/workflows/bridge-image.yml` matches
    - The bridge-image and ci-workflow tests pass; actionlint reports nothing
  </acceptance_criteria>
  <done>The Bridge pin can move with Proton's releases, and every move is built and smoke-tested before it can merge.</done>
</task>

</tasks>

<threat_model>
## Trust Boundaries

| Boundary | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| owner -> config.yaml pin | Whoever edits the pin decides which Bridge the worker talks to |
| Renovate PR -> bridge/Dockerfile | Automated change to a pinned supply-chain input |

## STRIDE Threat Register

| Threat ID | Category | Component | Severity | Disposition | Mitigation Plan |
|-----------|----------|-----------|----------|-------------|-----------------|
| T-02-SC | Tampering | Renovate-proposed Bridge bumps | medium | mitigate | Tag plus commit bumped together; the Dockerfile's commit check fails a mismatched bump; CI builds and smoke-tests each PR; the owner merges |
| T-02-50 | Spoofing | Blindly accepting an attacker's certificate | high | mitigate | The command never writes trust; the owner compares two independent readings (init output inside the Bridge container, and what the worker sees) before editing config (D-73) |
| T-02-51 | Information Disclosure | Credentials sent while inspecting an unknown certificate | high | mitigate | Uses capturePeerCertificate only, whose connection carries nothing beyond STARTTLS and the TLS handshake (wire-tested in 02-18, D-80); static check that the command never calls openImap |
| T-02-52 | Elevation of Privilege | Renovate managing unrelated dependencies against the repo's age gate | low | mitigate | enabledManagers limited to the custom regex manager |
</threat_model>

<verification>
- `scripts/test-imap.sh up && pnpm vitest run apps/worker/test/bridge-trust.test.ts apps/worker/test/bridge-image.test.ts apps/worker/test/cli.test.ts apps/worker/test/ci-workflow.test.ts` passes
- `actionlint .github/workflows/bridge-image.yml` reports nothing
</verification>

<success_criteria>
- D-73: the owner sees the fingerprint the worker sees and pastes it themselves; nothing is trusted automatically
- D-31: the Bridge pin is bumped automatically, as tag plus commit, and verified by CI
</success_criteria>

## Artifacts this phase produces (this plan's share)

- Files: `apps/worker/src/commands/bridge-trust.ts`, `apps/worker/test/bridge-trust.test.ts`, `renovate.json`, `.github/workflows/bridge-image.yml`; modified `apps/worker/src/command.ts`, `apps/worker/test/cli.test.ts`, `apps/worker/test/bridge-image.test.ts`
- CLI: `sift bridge trust <slug>`
- CI workflow: `bridge-image`

## Flagged assumptions

- A2: Renovate's github-tags datasource fills currentDigest with the tag's commit SHA (Bridge v3 tags are lightweight). If not, the first bump PR fails the build's commit check, and the config needs a separate digest lookup.

