must_haves:
  truths:
    - "openImap with tls { mode: 'starttls', pinSha256 } logs in to the Dovecot test server end to end: it captures the presented certificate on a credential-free handshake, compares its SPKI fingerprint with the pin, and logs in over a second connection verified twice, by `ca: [captured PEM]` and by a checkServerIdentity that re-checks the SPKI pin and ignores the hostname (D-40, D-73, D-80)"
    - "On the capture connection the server receives nothing beyond STARTTLS and the TLS handshake: in starttls mode exactly one plaintext line (`<tag> STARTTLS`), in implicit mode none, and zero bytes of IMAP data after the handshake (no login command, no CAPABILITY, no LOGOUT). A wire-level test with a recording fake server proves it, in addition to the static grep (D-80)"
    - "capture.ts is the only module under apps/worker/src that turns certificate verification off. Its header comment cites D-80, the durable record of that exception (02-CONTEXT.md D-80, the resolved Open Question 2 in 02-RESEARCH.md and the D-80 entry in the .wolf/cerebrum.md Decision Log)"
    - "A server that presents a different certificate on the login connection than on the capture fails the login connection before any credential is sent: an unrelated self-signed certificate fails the chain check (class cert_untrusted), and a certificate issued by the captured one passes the chain but fails the SPKI re-check (class pin_mismatch). In both cases, in starttls and implicit mode, the server receives no login command and no IMAP data after the handshake (D-80)"
    - "The captured certificate lives in memory only: openImap captures afresh on every call, including after a pin mismatch or a certificate error, keeps nothing between calls, and neither capture.ts nor connect.ts imports a filesystem module or writes a file (D-73, D-80)"
    - "With a pin that differs from the presented certificate, openImap fails with PinMismatchError (class pin_mismatch, `seen` = the presented fingerprint) before any IMAP client is created (D-40, D-73)"
    - "Without a pin, openImap keeps Node's default chain and hostname verification, so a self-signed server fails with class cert_untrusted, never a silent connect (D-74)"
    - "tls.mode starttls requires the STARTTLS upgrade (`doSTARTTLS: true`), and implicit uses TLS from the first byte; a server whose greeting offers no STARTTLS fails with class no_starttls, and neither the capture nor openImap sends it a login command (D-42, D-74)"
    - "classifyImapError maps refused/unknown-host/reset/closed to unreachable, timeouts to timeout, authenticationFailed to auth_rejected, the pin error to pin_mismatch, chain errors to cert_untrusted and the STARTTLS-missing error to no_starttls"
