    - .wolf/cerebrum.md Decision Log (the D-80 entry) and Do-Not-Repeat (negative greps scan comments; sockets need resume())
    - node_modules/imapflow/dist/esm/imap-flow.js: how the `tls` option reaches tls.connect on the implicit connection and on the STARTTLS upgrade, and the doSTARTTLS refusal
  </read_first>
  <action>
1. `capture.ts`: implement the interfaces block with node:net and node:tls, per D-80.
   - Bound every step by timeoutMs (default 10000). Call `socket.resume()` while reading the greeting and the tagged STARTTLS reply.
   - Detect STARTTLS support from the greeting's capability code only. Never send a capability request: the only command this module ever writes is the single STARTTLS line.
   - Pass `servername` only when the host is a name, not an IP address.
   - After reading the certificate, destroy the socket at once. Do not send a logout or anything else.
   - Header comment, citing D-80 as the durable decision (02-CONTEXT.md D-80 and the cerebrum Decision Log): the governing rule is "never send credentials or data over an unverified connection"; this handshake has verification off only so it can read the presented certificate and compare it with the owner's pin; it carries nothing but STARTTLS and the TLS handshake; the login connection in connect.ts verifies the same certificate again. Comments say "credentials" or "login commands" and never spell an IMAP authentication command name in capitals, because the acceptance grep scans comments too.
   - Keep no module-level state: the certificate is returned to the caller and dropped with the socket.
2. `connect.ts`: implement the interfaces block.
   - starttls mode uses `secure: false, doSTARTTLS: true`; implicit uses `secure: true`.
   - With `tls.pinSha256`: call `(deps.capture ?? capturePeerCertificate)` with host, port, mode and a timeout. On a fingerprint mismatch throw PinMismatchError before creating the ImapFlow client. Otherwise pass `tls: { ca: [captured.pem], minVersion: 'TLSv1.2', checkServerIdentity }`, where checkServerIdentity returns undefined only when peerSpkiSha256(cert) equals the pin and ignores the hostname (D-40); anything else returns an Error with code SIFT_TLS_PIN_MISMATCH. The connection that carries the password is therefore verified twice: chain against the captured certificate, then the SPKI pin (D-80).
   - The captured PEM is a local of this one call. Nothing is cached between calls, so every reconnect and every retry after a certificate error captures again (D-80).
   - Without a pin: `tls: { minVersion: 'TLSv1.2' }`, so Node's default chain and hostname verification applies (D-74).
   - Always `logger: false`, `disableAutoIdle: true` (polling only, D-27), `clientInfo: { name: 'Sift' }`, `connectionTimeout` and `greetingTimeout` from connectTimeoutMs (default 15000), `socketTimeout: 120000`, and `disableAutoEnable` passed through.
   - Construct the client through deps.createClient (default `new ImapFlow(o)`), await `client.connect()`, and on failure closeImap then rethrow the original error.
   - Never pass any option that turns verification off in this file.
   - `classifyImapError` walks `cause` up to 5 levels checking `code` and `authenticationFailed`. It never inspects or returns message text that could hold credentials.
3. `imap-connect.test.ts`, tracer case: requireTestImap(); a fresh user; openImap with `tls: { mode: 'starttls', pinSha256: await testImapPin() }` and TEST_IMAP.password; `mailboxOpen('INBOX', { readOnly: true })` returns a numeric uidValidity; closeImap resolves.
  </action>
  <verify>
    <automated>scripts/test-imap.sh up && pnpm vitest run apps/worker/test/imap-connect.test.ts && pnpm typecheck</automated>
    <fails_when>non-zero exit; "test IMAP server ready" never printed; the pinned login against Dovecot failing (for example because the STARTTLS upgrade dropped `ca` or `checkServerIdentity`); or TS errors</fails_when>
  </verify>
  <acceptance_criteria>
    - `grep -c 'doSTARTTLS: true' apps/worker/src/imap/connect.ts` prints 1
    - `grep -n 'capturePeerCertificate' apps/worker/src/imap/connect.ts` matches
    - `grep -n 'D-80' apps/worker/src/imap/capture.ts` matches (the header comment cites the durable decision, not plan notes)
    - The tracer case in imap-connect.test.ts passes against the Dovecot test server
  </acceptance_criteria>
  <done>The worker can log in to a self-signed STARTTLS server through capture, pin comparison and a doubly verified login connection, end to end against a real server.</done>
</task>

