.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:103:bridge/entrypoint.sh modes (argument 1, default serve):
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:105:                log the presented certificate's SPKI fingerprint in the background, exec bridge --noninteractive as uid 1000
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:109:Process model: the entrypoint runs as root under tini; every gpg/pass/socat/bridge process runs as uid 1000 (user `bridge`) via `setpriv --reuid=1000 --regid=1000 --init-groups`. Root is kept only so 02-08's init can write the bind-mounted .env.mailboxes in place with its host owner and mode intact.
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:110:Container paths: /data (sift-bridge volume: HOME, GNUPGHOME=/data/.gnupg, PASSWORD_STORE_DIR=/data/.password-store, XDG_CONFIG_HOME=/data/config, XDG_DATA_HOME=/data/data, XDG_CACHE_HOME=/data/cache), /run/user/1000 (gpg-agent socket dir).
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:111:Only in the bridge-init service (D-79, D-81): /run/sift/.env.mailboxes (mailbox env file, read-write), /run/sift/config (config dir, read-only) and /run/sift/.env.mailboxes.bak (the host's pre-created backup file, read-write). In the bridge service none of these paths exists.
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:112:SPKI fingerprint format (shared with apps/worker/src/imap/pin.ts in 02-04 and the config value imap.tls.pin_sha256 in 02-02): base64 of sha256 over the DER SubjectPublicKeyInfo, i.e. `openssl x509 -pubkey -noout | openssl pkey -pubin -outform DER | openssl dgst -sha256 -binary | openssl base64 -A` (44 characters ending in `=`).
