.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:150:1. `bridge/Dockerfile` (RESEARCH Pattern 1, trial-built in research). Header comment: what the image is, that `apps/worker/test/bridge-image.test.ts` pins it, and that Renovate bumps BRIDGE_VERSION and BRIDGE_COMMIT together (D-31).
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:152:   - The three pin lines must be adjacent, in this order, because plan 02-15's Renovate regex matches them as one block: `# renovate: datasource=github-tags depName=ProtonMail/proton-bridge`, then `ARG BRIDGE_VERSION=v3.27.0`, then `ARG BRIDGE_COMMIT=04e46eb4fbc1c7ef4425a920bfc352050da0606b`.
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:154:   - `git clone --depth 1 --branch "${BRIDGE_VERSION}"` of `https://github.com/ProtonMail/proton-bridge.git` into /src, then `test "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" = "${BRIDGE_COMMIT}"` in the same RUN so a moved tag fails the build.
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:157:   - Copy only `/src/bridge` to `/usr/local/bin/bridge`. Never copy the launcher binary: it is the self-update path that D-30 disables.
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:158:   - `useradd -m -u 1000 bridge`; `install -d -o bridge -g bridge -m 0700 /data /run/user/1000`; `install -d -m 0755 /run/sift`.
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:161:2. `bridge/entrypoint.sh` (`#!/bin/bash`, `set -euo pipefail`). Follow the interfaces block exactly.
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:163:   - Helper `as_bridge` runs a command via `setpriv --reuid=1000 --regid=1000 --init-groups` with those variables set.
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:165:   - `keychain_init` is idempotent. It writes `$GNUPGHOME/gpg-agent.conf` with `allow-preset-passphrase`, `max-cache-ttl 34560000` and `default-cache-ttl 34560000`. When no secret key exists it runs `gpg --batch --pinentry-mode loopback --passphrase-fd 0 --quick-gen-key sift-bridge-vault rsa3072 encr never`, feeding the passphrase on stdin (never as an argument). Then `pass init <fingerprint>`, then `pass insert -m sift/canary` with a fixed non-secret marker text.
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:167:     - If no secret key exists, print `Bridge is not initialised: run docker compose run --rm bridge-init` and exit 78.
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:170:     - Refuse an insecure vault: if `/data/config/protonmail/bridge-v3/insecure` exists, print `Insecure Bridge vault found; Sift refuses to run it. Remove the sift-bridge volume and run docker compose run --rm bridge-init again` and exit 78.
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:173:   - `print_fingerprint`: wait up to 60 s for 127.0.0.1:1143, capture the certificate with `openssl s_client -starttls imap -connect 127.0.0.1:1143 </dev/null | openssl x509 -outform PEM`, then print `Bridge certificate SHA-256 (public key): <fingerprint>` (the value owners pin, D-73). Write no file.
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:177:     - Start print_fingerprint in the background, then `exec` `bridge --noninteractive` through as_bridge.
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:178:     - Serve mode never reads /run/sift/.env.mailboxes or /run/sift/config; in the bridge service those paths do not exist (D-79).
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:182:3. `compose.yaml`: add the `bridge` service and the `sift-bridge` volume exactly as in the interfaces block (RESEARCH "Compose service shape", without the certificate volume).
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:185:   - `restart: unless-stopped`. Do not add `depends_on: bridge` to the worker (D-32).
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:186:   - The bridge service mounts only `sift-bridge:/data`, with a comment: it never sees .env.mailboxes or config; the one-shot bridge-init service (added in Task 2) is the only service that does (D-39, D-79).
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:188:     - Before the first `docker compose up`, run `docker volume create sift-bridge`. Compose v2.2.3 fails every command while an external volume is missing (Pitfall 3).
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:191:4. `.env.example`: add `SIFT_BRIDGE_KEYCHAIN_PASSPHRASE=` with a comment. Generate it with `openssl rand -hex 24`. Only the bridge container receives it. It unlocks the GPG key that protects Bridge's session vault in the sift-bridge volume, so a copied volume is useless without it. Losing it means running `docker compose run --rm bridge-init` again. Also add a commented `# SIFT_BRIDGE_PORT=1143`.
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:193:   - Run `docker volume create sift-bridge`.
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:195:6. `scripts/bridge-smoke.sh` (`set -euo pipefail`). Run it from the repo root; env BRIDGE_SMOKE_PORT (default 11143) and SIFT_BRIDGE_IMAGE (default sift-bridge:local).
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:196:   - `docker build -t "$image" bridge`.
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-01-PLAN.md:197:   - Create a throwaway volume `sift-bridge-smoke-<random>`, with an EXIT trap that removes containers and the volume.
