.planning/phases/01-foundation-and-isolation/01-CONTEXT.md:19:- **D-01:** Phase 1 creates every M1 table now with minimal columns: `mailbox`, `mailbox_status`, `message`, `label`, `decision`, `folder_sync`, `label_event`, `rule_set`. Later phases add columns via migrations. The RLS test covers every table from day one.
.planning/phases/01-foundation-and-isolation/01-CONTEXT.md:25:- **D-07:** New `mailbox_status` table holds worker runtime state, one row per mailbox: `mailbox_id` is PK and FK; columns `state` (ok / error / disabled), `last_error`, `last_sync_at`, `last_seen_at`. It is mailbox-scoped like any other table (RLS, `sift_app` may write, covered by the catalog test). The worker never updates `mailbox`.
.planning/phases/01-foundation-and-isolation/01-CONTEXT.md:70:- **D-42:** `withMailbox(mailboxId, fn)` in `packages/db` opens a transaction and calls `set_config('app.mailbox_id', id, true)` (transaction-local), so pooled connections never carry a mailbox between uses. App code never receives a raw transaction or the raw pool; the scoped API is the enforcement for ISO-04.
.planning/phases/01-foundation-and-isolation/01-CONTEXT.md:73:- **D-45:** `withMailbox` does isolation only: it scopes any existing mailbox, disabled or not. "Disabled" is enforced elsewhere: the worker scheduler starts loops only for enabled mailboxes and rechecks the registry each tick; processing entry points (ingest, classify, apply labels) call `requireActive(scope)` (or pass `{ requireActive: true }`), which throws if `disabled_at` is set. Reading status and history does not.
.planning/phases/01-foundation-and-isolation/01-CONTEXT.md:85:  | Reused connection after a previous `withMailbox` | Reads return nothing, no error (the `nullif` case) |
.planning/phases/01-foundation-and-isolation/01-CONTEXT.md:89:- **D-49:** The worker runs the real scheduler skeleton with a no-op per-mailbox batch: after startup checks (env, config, drift), a supervisor ticks, rereads the registry, starts/stops mailbox tasks, touches the heartbeat file, and coordinates shutdown. Each due mailbox runs as its own async task; the Phase 1 batch updates `mailbox_status.last_seen_at` (and `last_sync_at` / state on success). Phase 2 drops ingest into this loop.
.planning/phases/01-foundation-and-isolation/01-CONTEXT.md:91:- **D-51:** A failing mailbox run sets `mailbox_status.state = error` with a redacted `last_error` (no secrets) and backs off exponentially (capped, e.g. 15 min); the next success sets `ok`. Mailbox failures are visible in `mailbox_status`, not in container health.
.planning/phases/01-foundation-and-isolation/01-CONTEXT.md:107:      imap: { host, port, username, password_env, folder }   # folder defaults to INBOX
.planning/phases/01-foundation-and-isolation/01-CONTEXT.md:158:- `docs/adr/0003-traces-and-mail-app-relabels.md` — context for `decision`, `folder_sync`, `label_event` tables that Phase 1 creates minimally
.planning/phases/01-foundation-and-isolation/01-CONTEXT.md:184:- Phase 2 plugs IMAP ingest into the worker's per-mailbox batch (D-49) and extends `message` / `folder_sync` via migrations through the scoped API (D-43).
.planning/phases/01-foundation-and-isolation/01-CONTEXT.md:195:- `withMailbox` has one job (isolation); "disabled" is the scheduler's and `requireActive`'s job.
