.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-08-PLAN.md:26:    - "`configure` mode on a fresh, keychain-initialised volume starts Bridge with its gRPC frontend, turns telemetry and automatic updates off and reads them back as off, prints the certificate fingerprint with the line to paste into config.yaml (`pin_sha256: <fingerprint>` under the mailbox's imap.tls), and exits 3 with `no Bridge account is logged in` (D-39, D-73, PROJECT no-telemetry)"
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-08-PLAN.md:27:    - "For each configured mailbox whose imap.username (case-insensitive) is one of a Bridge account's addresses, the helper upserts `<password_env>=<Bridge IMAP password>` into the mounted .env.mailboxes: an existing line is replaced in place, other lines and comments are kept, the file is written in place (the existing file is opened, truncated and written; never a temp file plus rename), so it keeps its inode, mode and host owner, and only `wrote <NAME> to .env.mailboxes (mailbox \"<slug>\")` is printed (D-39, D-81)"
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-08-PLAN.md:28:    - "Before the first write, the previous content of .env.mailboxes is written in place into the owner's pre-created `.env.mailboxes.bak` next to the original (bind-mounted at /run/sift/.env.mailboxes.bak, D-81), mode 0600, never in the sift-bridge volume, and configure prints `backup of the previous file: .env.mailboxes.bak (next to .env.mailboxes)`. If the backup target is missing or not a regular file, no password is written either: exit 2 with a message naming `touch .env.mailboxes.bak && chmod 600 .env.mailboxes.bak` (D-39, D-79, D-81)"
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-08-PLAN.md:29:    - "Neither .env.mailboxes nor .env.mailboxes.bak is ever replaced: the helper never uses a temp file, a rename or the create flag on them, and after a write both files keep their inode (Go tests on real files, plus a static check over bridge/helper) (D-81)"
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-08-PLAN.md:31:    - "`docker compose run --rm bridge-init` creates the keychain if absent, attaches the owner's terminal to Bridge's own CLI for `login` (password and 2FA typed without echo), then runs configure; without a TTY it refuses with a fixed message and exit 2 (D-36, D-72, D-79)"
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-08-PLAN.md:32:    - "init and configure refuse with exit 2 and `create .env.mailboxes first: cp .env.mailboxes.example .env.mailboxes` when /run/sift/.env.mailboxes is not a regular file (Pitfall 4); when the path does not exist at all (the mode was started in the bridge service, which has no such mount) they refuse with exit 2 and `run this in the bridge-init service: docker compose run --rm bridge-init` (D-79)"
