.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-08-PLAN.md:277:- Resolved by D-81: the owner pre-creates `.env.mailboxes.bak` (`touch .env.mailboxes.bak && chmod 600 .env.mailboxes.bak`, README quick start), and 02-01 bind-mounts it into bridge-init only, in long syntax, at /run/sift/.env.mailboxes.bak. A probe on this machine's Compose v2.2.3 (neutral file name) showed that a rename onto a bind-mounted file fails with `Device or resource busy`, and an in-place truncate-and-write keeps the host inode and mode, which is why both files are written in place.
