.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-RESEARCH.md:503:**Why:** `constants.Host = "127.0.0.1"` is a constant used by both listeners [VERIFIED: internal/constants/constants.go:70-71; services/imapsmtpserver/listener.go:30-38]. Linux refuses a wildcard bind on a port already bound on 127.0.0.1 [VERIFIED: probe output above].
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-RESEARCH.md:505:**Warning signs:** the healthcheck is green but the worker gets `ECONNREFUSED` on `bridge:1143`.
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-RESEARCH.md:513:**How to avoid:** The README quick start adds `docker volume create sift-bridge` before the first `up`. compose-smoke uses `${SIFT_BRIDGE_VOLUME:-sift-bridge}`-style naming and creates its own (mirror the `SIFT_PGDATA_VOLUME` pattern). `compose.test.ts` asserts the name variable. It is the same class of problem as the existing `.env.mailboxes` env_file trap (cerebrum).
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-RESEARCH.md:517:**How to avoid:** Write in place (`open(O_WRONLY|O_TRUNC)` + fsync) after the backup exists on the host. Either a host-side wrapper makes the backup and checks preconditions (file exists, is a regular file, mode 0600) before `docker compose run --rm bridge init`, or a second pre-created file is bind-mounted for the backup. This is an open question for the planner (see Open Questions).
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-RESEARCH.md:532:**What goes wrong:** ImapFlow returns `uidValidity` and `highestModseq` as `bigint`, and `uidNext` as `number` [VERIFIED: imapflow dist/esm/types.d.ts:175-181]. JSON logging throws on bigint, and a Postgres `integer` overflows above 2^31 (UIDs and UIDVALIDITY are unsigned 32-bit [CITED: RFC 3501 §2.3.1.1]).
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-RESEARCH.md:540:**How to avoid:** Treat it as a retryable mailbox error (backoff). The next run's EXAMINE sees the new UIDVALIDITY. Never advance `folder_sync` outside a committed chunk.
