.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-DISCUSSION-LOG.md:7:**Phase:** 02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-DISCUSSION-LOG.md:90:**Notes:** Prefix keys `mid:` / `hdr:` (and `pm:` if the spike finds a stable Proton internal ID); a conflict is "same message" (upsert adding a location), and the spike counts real collisions (add a Date tiebreaker if meaningful); conservative normalisation (strip brackets/whitespace, lowercase domain only); `message_location` table with `UNIQUE (mailbox_id, folder, uidvalidity, uid)`; resync replaces a folder's location rows and leaves messages, labels and decisions untouched.
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-DISCUSSION-LOG.md:153:**Notes:** Build from source (`ProtonMail/proton-bridge`), self-update off, Renovate bumps tag + SHA together.
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-DISCUSSION-LOG.md:162:**Notes:** SPKI pin with a custom `checkServerIdentity` that ignores the hostname; init exports the cert to a shared volume (worker read-only); a changed cert fails closed and points at `sift bridge trust`; STARTTLS required with no plaintext fallback, with a fake-server test.
