.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-04-PLAN.md:121:1. `scripts/test-imap.sh {up|down|status}` (`set -euo pipefail`):
.planning/phases/02-bridge-spike-and-imap-ingest/02-04-PLAN.md:122:   - `up` reuses a running `sift-test-imap` container. Otherwise it runs `docker run -d --name sift-test-imap -p 127.0.0.1:${SIFT_TEST_IMAP_PORT:-31143}:31143 -e USER_PASSWORD=sift-test-password dovecot/dovecot:2.4.5`. Confirm the image's dev-mode variables, ports and TLS certificate path in the image documentation (doc.dovecot.org "Docker"). If the image does not generate its own certificate, create a CA:true self-signed one with `openssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:2048 -nodes -days 30 -subj /CN=sift-test-imap -addext basicConstraints=critical,CA:TRUE` into a mktemp dir and mount it at the documented path. Then poll for up to 60 s until `openssl s_client -starttls imap -connect 127.0.0.1:<port>` prints a certificate. Finally print `test IMAP server ready on 127.0.0.1:<port>`.
